WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:15.713
Miss Minchin turned white with rage.

2
00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:21.375
"I'll throw Sara out of the school!" she cried to Mr. Barrow, the lawyer.

3
00:00:21.376 --> 00:00:24.353
Mr. Barrow had moved toward the door.

4
00:00:24.354 --> 00:00:30.671
"I wouldn't do that, madam," he replied. "People will think you're cruel.

5
00:00:30.672 --> 00:00:34.522
They won't want to send their daughters to the school."

6
00:00:34.523 --> 00:00:38.784
Miss Minchin knew that Mr. Barrow was a clever businessman.

7
00:00:38.785 --> 00:00:42.524
And she herself was a shrewd businesswoman.

8
00:00:42.525 --> 00:00:47.164
"So what should I do with her?" she asked Mr. Barrow.

9
00:00:47.165 --> 00:00:53.837
"Keep her. She's a clever child. You can get a lot of work from her before she grows older."

10
00:00:53.838 --> 00:00:59.913
"I will get a lot of work out of her before she's older!" exclaimed Miss Minchin.

11
00:00:59.914 --> 00:01:06.320
"I'm sure you will," said Mr. Barrow with an evil smile. "Good day."

12
00:01:06.321 --> 00:01:11.022
As the lawyer left, Miss Amelia came into the schoolroom.

13
00:01:11.023 --> 00:01:17.024
Miss Amelia took a step backward when she saw the furious face of her sister.

14
00:01:17.025 --> 00:01:21.549
"Does Sara have a black dress?" demanded Miss Minchin.

15
00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:27.020
"Yes, but it's too small for her now," said Miss Amelia, trembling.

16
00:01:27.021 --> 00:01:31.440
"Tell her to put it on anyway!" Miss Minchin said fiercely.

17
00:01:31.441 --> 00:01:37.206
"And tell her that her father has died. Then send her to me!"

18
00:01:37.207 --> 00:01:44.404
Miss Amelia gasped and sat down in a nearby chair. "Captain Crewe is dead?"

19
00:01:44.405 --> 00:01:48.652
"Yes, and he has died without a penny," said Miss Minchin.

20
00:01:48.653 --> 00:01:52.930
"That spoiled, daydreaming child is left a pauper in my care.

21
00:01:52.931 --> 00:01:59.358
I'm getting rid of her carriage, her maid, and that huge birthday doll at once. Now go tell her!"

22
00:01:59.359 --> 00:02:04.614
"But . . . Must I tell her now?" Miss Amelia asked.

23
00:02:04.615 --> 00:02:09.187
"This moment! Don't sit staring like a goose! Go!"

24
00:02:09.188 --> 00:02:12.331
Miss Amelia felt sorry for Sara.

25
00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:16.956
But she didn't dare to disobey her sister. She hurried away.

26
00:02:16.957 --> 00:02:19.819
Miss Minchin paced around the room.

27
00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:25.490
All year she'd been dreaming about Captain Crewe's diamond mines.

28
00:02:25.491 --> 00:02:28.957
She'd imagined a fortune being left to the school.

29
00:02:28.958 --> 00:02:34.683
And now, instead of looking forward to a gift from him, she would have nothing.

30
00:02:34.684 --> 00:02:38.556
"Princess Sara indeed!" she muttered.

31
00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:42.732
As she swept past the table, Miss Minchin heard a noise.

32
00:02:42.733 --> 00:02:45.673
It sounded like someone crying.

33
00:02:45.674 --> 00:02:49.662
She pulled up the tablecloth. There was Becky!

34
00:02:49.663 --> 00:02:55.936
"How dare you!" cried Miss Minchin. "You've been listening!"

35
00:02:55.937 --> 00:03:00.499
"I didn't mean to, ma'am!" Becky desperately tried to explain.

36
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:06.737
"Poor Miss Sara. How will she manage without a maid? Please, may I wait on her?"

37
00:03:06.738 --> 00:03:11.471
"No. She's a servant now," Miss Minchin snapped.

38
00:03:11.472 --> 00:03:14.389
"She'll wait on other people."

39
00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:18.148
Meanwhile Miss Amelia spoke to Sara.

40
00:03:18.149 --> 00:03:23.290
The little girl refused to show any emotion in front of Miss Amelia.

41
00:03:23.291 --> 00:03:26.820
She ran to her room.

42
00:03:26.821 --> 00:03:31.752
"My papa is dead!" she kept repeating in horror.

43
00:03:31.753 --> 00:03:35.074
Finally Sara put on her black dress.

44
00:03:35.075 --> 00:03:39.333
She picked up Emily and went to see Miss Minchin.

45
00:03:39.334 --> 00:03:42.592
"Put down your doll," said Miss Minchin.

46
00:03:42.593 --> 00:03:49.689
"No," Sara replied. "She's all I have. My papa gave her to me."

47
00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:55.400
Miss Minchin glared at Sara. "You'll have no time for dolls now.

48
00:03:55.401 --> 00:04:00.797
You will have to work and improve yourself and make yourself useful."

49
00:04:00.798 --> 00:04:03.649
Sara looked almost relieved.

50
00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:07.906
"Working will make things easier to bear," she said.

51
00:04:07.907 --> 00:04:12.734
"You'll do whatever you're told," Miss Minchin said.

52
00:04:12.735 --> 00:04:15.661
"You'll run errands and help in the kitchen.

53
00:04:15.662 --> 00:04:19.148
You'll help the younger children with their French lessons."

54
00:04:19.149 --> 00:04:22.722
"Oh, I can do that!" exclaimed Sara.

55
00:04:22.723 --> 00:04:27.723
The headmistress looked stern. "Everything will be different now.

56
00:04:27.724 --> 00:04:33.598
And if you don't please me, you'll be sent away. Remember that. Now go."

57
00:04:33.599 --> 00:04:35.341
Sara turned to leave.

58
00:04:35.342 --> 00:04:41.445
"Stop!" said Miss Minchin. "Aren't you going to thank me?"

59
00:04:41.446 --> 00:04:44.823
"What for?" asked Sara.

60
00:04:44.824 --> 00:04:49.277
"For my kindness in giving you a home."

61
00:04:49.278 --> 00:04:55.159
Dark thoughts had filled Sara's heart. Slowly, she took a deep breath.

62
00:04:55.160 --> 00:05:01.639
"You are not kind, and this is not a home."

63
00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:03.757
Sara ran out of the room.

64
00:05:03.758 --> 00:05:07.484
All she wanted to do was go to her room and think.

65
00:05:07.485 --> 00:05:10.527
But Miss Amelia was standing at her door.

66
00:05:10.528 --> 00:05:14.640
"This isn't your room now," said Miss Amelia.

67
00:05:14.641 --> 00:05:19.206
She was following Miss Minchin's orders, but she didn't like them.

68
00:05:19.207 --> 00:05:22.923
"Where is my room?" asked Sara.

69
00:05:22.924 --> 00:05:26.947
"In the attic next to Becky's room."

70
00:05:26.948 --> 00:05:32.319
Sara slowly climbed the stairs to the attic.

71
00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:36.545
She opened the door to a different world from downstairs.

72
00:05:36.546 --> 00:05:42.124
Her new room had a slanting ceiling and a dingy skylight.

73
00:05:42.125 --> 00:05:46.713
The furniture looked worn and uncomfortable.

74
00:05:46.714 --> 00:05:50.216
Sara sat down on an old footstool.

75
00:05:50.217 --> 00:05:54.680
She hugged Emily tight, but she didn't cry.

76
00:05:54.681 --> 00:05:59.760
She just put her face on Emily and sat there, not making one sound.

77
00:05:59.761 --> 00:06:04.408
She was still sitting like that when Becky came in.

78
00:06:04.409 --> 00:06:07.861
The servant girl ran to Sara and hugged her.

79
00:06:07.862 --> 00:06:13.147
"Oh, Becky!" said Sara, at last letting out a sob.

80
00:06:13.148 --> 00:06:17.481
"I told you we were the same—just two children.

81
00:06:17.482 --> 00:06:21.065
I'm not a princess anymore."

82
00:06:21.066 --> 00:06:31.568
"Yes, you are, Miss Sara!" Becky sobbed. "You'll always be a princess!"
